      "writtenOn": "2026-01-29T01:57:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This driver is not part of GKI builds (CONFIG_DRM_XE is not enabled by arch/x86/configs/gki_defconfig). We normally don\u0027t take patches for vendor modules since we neither build nor test them. Can this be applied on a downstream branch where vendor modules are built? Or should it be enabled as a GKI module instead of a vendor module so it is part of the GKI builds?",
      "revId": "05a27c9e5d2e97d5e429178b5980781e10f99f4a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
