      "writtenOn": "2026-01-30T02:32:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I checked the 6.18 GKI kconfigs:\n\n```\nINTEL_MEI\u003dy\nINTEL_MEI_ME\u003dy\nINTEL_MEI_*\u003dn (includes all ME client drivers)\n```\n\nThe first two configs build the ME PCI and client bus driver into the GKI kernel.\n\nThe disabled configs (which we enable alongside i915/Xe) are clients registered to that bus.\n\nI don\u0027t know if there\u0027s utility to providing the core in GKI without one or more client drivers, so I lean toward disabling the core in GKI builds.\n\nBut let me check with our Intel contacts to get their recommendation before proceeding.",
      "parentUuid": "295cc34b_c1ee6cfd",
      "revId": "05a27c9e5d2e97d5e429178b5980781e10f99f4a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
